# Signbee Document Signing & MCP Best Practices

Use this rule when integrating two-party e-signatures, generating NDAs/contracts from Markdown or PDF, configuring the Signbee MCP server (`signbee-mcp`), or calling the Signbee REST API (`https://signb.ee`).

## 1. Cursor Plugin, Agent Skill & MCP Configuration

### Cursor Plugin & Agent Skill
- **Cursor Plugin Repository**: `https://github.com/signbee/cursor-plugin`
- **Agent Skill Install**:
  ```bash
  npx skills add signbee/skill --skill signbee -g
  ```
- **LLM Documentation**: Fetch `https://signb.ee/llms.txt` (concise) or `https://signb.ee/llms-full.txt` (complete reference) before writing custom API wrappers.

### `.cursor/mcp.json` Setup (`signbee-mcp`)
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "signbee": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "signbee-mcp"],
      "env": {
        "SIGNBEE_API_KEY": "${env:SIGNBEE_API_KEY}"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## 2. Sending Documents for E-Signing (`POST /api/v1/send`)

- **Endpoint**: `POST https://signb.ee/api/v1/send`
- **Content Input**: Provide either `markdown` (auto-rendered into a formatted PDF) or `pdf_url` / base64 PDF payload.
- **Authentication**:
  - **With API Key (`Authorization: Bearer sb_live_...`)**: Immediately dispatches signing links to both parties without manual sender OTP.
  - **Keyless Mode (No API Key)**: Sends a 6-digit email OTP to `sender_email` first; call `POST https://signb.ee/api/v1/verify` with `document_id` and `otp` to confirm and dispatch.

### TypeScript Example
```typescript
export async function sendAgreementForSigning(params: {
  title: string;
  markdown: string;
  senderName: string;
  senderEmail: string;
  recipientName: string;
  recipientEmail: string;
  webhookUrl?: string;
}) {
  const response = await fetch("https://signb.ee/api/v1/send", {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
      ...(process.env.SIGNBEE_API_KEY
        ? { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.SIGNBEE_API_KEY}` }
        : {}),
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      title: params.title,
      markdown: params.markdown,
      sender_name: params.senderName,
      sender_email: params.senderEmail,
      recipient_name: params.recipientName,
      recipient_email: params.recipientEmail,
      webhook_url: params.webhookUrl,
    }),
  });

  if (!response.ok) {
    const err = await response.text();
    throw new Error(`Signbee API error (${response.status}): ${err}`);
  }

  return response.json() as Promise<{
    document_id: string;
    status: "pending_sender_verification" | "sent" | "completed";
    signing_url?: string;
  }>;
}
```

## 3. Status Polling & Webhook Handling

- Check document status via `GET https://signb.ee/api/v1/status/{document_id}`.
- Every completed PDF includes a tamper-evident **two-pass SHA-256 cryptographic signing certificate** appended to the final document.
- Never modify or re-compress a signed PDF buffer after completion, as doing so invalidates the SHA-256 document hash recorded on the certificate.
